---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SITE } from "@/consts";
---

<Layout title={SITE.TITLE} description={SITE.DESCRIPTION}>
  <main class="flex min-h-screen flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4">
    <h1 class="heading text-4xl uppercase">Accessibility Statement</h1>

    <div class="container space-y-4 px-22 text-lg text-secondary md:text-lg">
      <p class="text-secondary">
        I really care about creating usable and accessible digital spaces, so
        it'd be weird if I didn't do the same in this space.
      </p>
      <p>
        Accessibility is considered through the design and development process,
        with the goal of meeting WCAG 2.2 standards and regularly improving
        things like contrast, structure, keyboard, navigation, readability, and
        overall usability.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you experience any barriers or come across anything weird while using
        this site, please let me know. I'll do my best to handle it as soon as
        possible. I'm always trying to improve.
      </p>

      <p>Contact: <a href="mailto:hi@yessikenney.com">hi@yessikenney.com</a></p>
    </div>
    <hr />
    <p>Practice makes progress.</p>
    <a href="/" class="cursor-pointer underline">&larr; Go Back</a>
  </main>
</Layout>
